{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Design note (mechanism): code-review overlays receive per-prompt tools via the SHARED agent_runner provider seam (CodeReviewBatchRunner delegates each unit run to the passed agent_runner; batch_runner.py line ~92 'overlays follow the RUN's provider'), NOT a batch-runner-owned hook like plan-review's ProductionBatchRunner. So afe3 routes the Terraform seam via RunnerAgentStep.tool_provider (built by terraform_grounding.build_provider_and_sink from the assembled changed_files). The provider gates by prompt: code-review-iac (Round A/B) and code-review-verify get the two TF tools; base/coach/other overlays get none. changed_files also drives the externally-computed project_criteria passed into CodeReviewBatchRunner. Feature extracted to src/rebar/llm/code_review/terraform_grounding.py (152 LOC) to keep workflow_ops.py and gate_dispatch.py under the 800-LOC CI cap. All 7 ACs proven by held-out oracle (45 passed) through real production dispatch produce_code_review_verdict."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788556035746802001,"uuid":"33233e18-867a-44b1-9d51-7d7965fefa64"}